course: dictionary
lesson: 7368
title: Pleat: a fold in cloth
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: You can often work out a new word from the words around it. «The saguaro cactus's pleated stem swells like an accordion to store water.» The word accordion is a clue: an accordion folds in and out in neat lines, so pleated must mean folded in neat, even folds.
explain: A pleat is a fold made in cloth by doubling it over and pressing or sewing it in place. Skirts, school uniforms and kilts have pleats. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence: «its folded stem swells like an accordion». It still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: Pleat can also be a verb, meaning to make folds like this in cloth or paper. Children pleat paper to make fans and concertina books. Look at the words around it to tell which job the word is doing.
fact: A pleat is a fold made in cloth by doubling it over and pressing or sewing it in place.
fact: «Pleated» means having neat, even folds.
fact: To pleat means to make folds like this in cloth or paper.
fact: The saguaro cactus can grow over 12 metres tall and live over 150 years.
fact: Its pleated stem swells like an accordion to store water.
exercise: «Her pleated skirt swished as she ran.» What is a pleat? | A small hole in a sock | A bright coloured thread | *A fold made in cloth by doubling it over and pressing it
exercise: Children fold paper into pleats to make a fan. What does pleat mean here? | To paint the paper blue | *To make folds in the paper | To tear the paper into strips | To glue the paper flat
exercise: «The saguaro's pleated stem swells like an accordion.» What does pleated mean? | *Folded in neat, even folds | Cut into small pieces | Very thin and smooth | Painted bright green
test: «The kilt had many pleats.» What are pleats? | Loose threads at the hem | Holes made by moths | *Folds in cloth, pressed or sewn in place | Stripes of colour
test: Ravi will pleat the paper to make a concertina book. What does pleat mean here? | To glue the paper flat | To tear the paper | *To make folds in the paper | To draw a picture on the paper
exam: Which sentence uses pleat as a verb? | The school uniform is blue. | *Pleat the paper along the lines to make a fan. | The cactus grows in Arizona. | Her skirt has six pleats.
